& [ProviderSpecificFinding] is the llama.cpp and GPT-OSS boundary
  + [finding] is response_format constrained final JSON but did not itself give the model a semantic understanding of the intended field meanings
  + [required_instruction] is articulate the output field roles in the visible second-checkpoint instruction
  + [required_protocol] is preserve the prior assistant tool call, append the tool result, repeat the tool declaration, set tool_choice to none, and issue an explicit continuation checkpoint
  = caution: this observed recipe is provider-and-template evidence, not a universal tool-loop law

& [DesignConsequence] is the minimum Cantor inference seam now supported by evidence
  + [stage_1] is model identifies a need and emits typed Cantor parameters
  + [stage_2] is host validates authority and argument integrity
  + [stage_3] is Cantor returns a source-addressed semantic expression
  + [stage_4] is a new inference checkpoint imports the expression under an explicit output role contract
  + [stage_5] is host validates normalized meaning and records faults
  = consequence: Cantor can begin as an external checkpointed semantic coprocessor without modifying llama.cpp
  = next_gate: replace the hard-coded fixture with one minimal digest-bound signed semantic record lookup while preserving this exact harness boundary

